// ROUND 2026-09-17h ptrland — enumerate BY PROPERTY the functions that dispatch
// on LogosType::Kind and STEP an aggregate (Tuple/Array/Slice) while having NO
// `Ptr` arm at all. That absence is the defect class this round landed: a raw
// pointer TO a reference launders a borrow, and a grep cannot find it because
// AN ABSENCE HAS NO SPELLING.
// ⚠ ctx_of COARSENS to the enclosing function (the 2026-08-27 37-vs-0 finding),
// so this answers "which FUNCTIONS", and every row is read PER-SITE before it is
// believed. Cross-check reported beside the verdict.
// ⚠ CONTROL BUILT IN: this runs against the ARMED tree, where `type_is_ha` and
// `bc_holds_any_ref_type` HAVE gained a Ptr arm. If the rule is sound they must
// be ABSENT from no_ptr_arm while their unarmed siblings remain.
#include "cxx_schema.dl"
#include "lir_dispatch.dl"
target_enum(E) :- decl(E, "Enum", "logos::compiler::LogosType::Kind").

.decl steps_aggregate(fn: symbol)
.output steps_aggregate
steps_aggregate(F) :- tests(F, "Tuple", _).
steps_aggregate(F) :- tests(F, "Array", _).

.decl has_ptr_arm(fn: symbol)
.output has_ptr_arm
has_ptr_arm(F) :- tests(F, "Ptr", _).

.decl no_ptr_arm(fn: symbol)
.output no_ptr_arm
no_ptr_arm(F) :- steps_aggregate(F), !has_ptr_arm(F).
